            driveStory = "You are passing Freeman Field in Seymour, site of the historic 1945 civil rights protest by 101 Tuskegee Airmen officers that helped pave the way to military desegregation.",
            historyNerdDiscovery = "Between 1945 and 1946, Freeman Field was also America's primary intelligence depot for evaluating captured German and Japanese combat aircraft, storing over 16,000 tons of enemy equipment.",
